NAME

ulibMatchFidoNetAddress - Finds an AKA to match a zone


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibMatchFidoNetAddress(struct FidoNetAddress *Source,
                                           a0

                              struct FidoNetAddress *Dest)
                                           a1


DESCRIPTION

This function will search the configuration for a FidoNet address which has
<Source->Zone> as a zone number.  The configuration is searched in the
following order:

The XFIDONET:AKA.XLK file
Message section addresses (EchoMail/NetMail)
Primary addresses (from xenolink.cfg)
Any primary address

The matched address is returned in <Dest>,

This function is useful when it is not known which address to use as the
source address when generating mail to a destination; for example, if you
wished to send mail to 14:1/2, this function would return the Sysop's
zone 14 AKA (if the Sysop has one) or his default FidoNet address if not.


RETURNS

0 - Failure, no address found whatsoever
1 - Success, matched an address in AKA.XLK
2 - Success, matched a message section address
3 - Success, matched a primary address (from xenolink.cfg)
4 - Success, didn't match any of the above, and defaulted to the first
      available primary address
